{"day_done": 3, "slots": {"0": {"id": "E01", "name": "Ana", "role": "normal"}, "1": {"id": "E02", "name": "Ben", "role": "normal"}, "2": {"id": "E03", "name": "Chloe", "role": "normal"}, "3": {"id": "E04", "name": "Dev", "role": "normal"}, "4": {"id": "E05", "name": "Ellis", "role": "normal"}, "5": {"id": "E06", "name": "Farah", "role": "normal"}, "6": {"id": "E07", "name": "Gus", "role": "normal"}, "7": {"id": "E08", "name": "Hana", "role": "normal"}}, "diaries": {"E01": [[1, "Day 1 complete. Closed 2/2 (bonus earned). Alex's note (W-2) was crucial: ALD-118's bug was in `averages.py`, not the file named by the reproduce tool. Always trace imports when the main file delegates. ALD-125 was a genuine cannot-reproduce. Tomorrow: check helper files first for logic errors, use reproduce tool to verify before closing."], [2, "Day 2 complete. Closed 1/2 (target met). ALD-101 confirmed Alex's note (W-2): logic was in helper `text_rules.py`, not `slugs.py`. Fix was filtering empty strings from split. ALD-105 pending: reproduced in `calendar_days.py`. Saturday '2026-11-07' returns True, should be False. Didn't see code content before day end. Tomorrow: review `calendar_days.py` logic first thing and fix weekday check."], [3, "Day 3 complete. Closed 1/2 (target met). ALD-106 confirmed Alex's note (W-2) again: logic was in helper `dedupe.py`, not `tags.py`. Fix was case-insensitive comparison. ALD-119 pending: reproduced in `rota.py`. Week 1 returns 'Ben' (index 1) instead of 'Ana' (index 0). Looks like off-by-one error. Tomorrow: fix index calculation in `rota.py` first thing."]], "E02": [[1, "Closed ALD-101. The bug was in helper `text_rules.py`, not the file reproduce named. Alex's wiki note was right\u2014check helpers first.\nALD-111 still open. `previews.py` truncate function exceeds limit. Limit includes the ellipsis (10 chars total). Current code cuts text at limit then adds dots.\nTomorrow: Finish ALD-111 first."], [2, "Day 2: Closed ALD-119. The bug was in helper `cycles.py`, not the file reproduce named. Week indexing was off by one.\nALD-104 still open. `durations.py` parse_duration returns 60 for '1h30m'. Parses hours but drops minutes.\nTomorrow: Finish ALD-104 first."], [3, "Day 3: Closed ALD-105. The bug was in helper `weekdays.py`, called by `calendar_days.py`. Saturday counted as business day (weekday < 6 instead of < 5).\nALD-110 still open. `ticket_ids.py` next_ticket_id returns existing ID. Input ['ALD-9', 'ALD-10'] expected 'ALD-11' got 'ALD-10'.\nTomorrow: Finish ALD-110 first. Check helpers if `ticket_ids.py` uses any."]], "E03": [[1, "Day 1: 2/2 closed. Alex's tip was key for ALD-106\u2014the bug was in the helper (dedupe.py), not the file named by reproduce. Check helpers first. ALD-125 passed immediately; always run reproduce before coding to catch non-issues. Remember case-insensitivity for tag merging."], [2, "Day 2: 1/2 closed. ALD-112 confirmed Alex's tip\u2014bug was in the helper (csv_split.py), not the file reproduce named. ALD-102 carries over: pages.paginate returns [3, 4] instead of [1, 2] for page 1. Suspect off-by-one error in the slice start index. Start there tomorrow."], [3, "Day 3: 1/2 closed. ALD-118 confirmed Alex's tip again\u2014bug was in the helper (averages.py), dividing by len(values) instead of sum(weights). ALD-116 carries over: running_total accumulates state across calls ([1,3,5] instead of [5]). Suspect mutable default argument in totals.py. Check function signature first tomorrow."]], "E04": [[1, "Day 1: 2 tickets closed (ALD-105 fixed, ALD-125 cannot_reproduce). Bonus earned.\nLesson: Check helper files when the main file delegates (like weekdays.py). Alex's note was correct.\nProcess: If reproduce tool passes (expected == got), close as cannot_reproduce immediately. Saves steps.\nGoal: Aim for 2 closes again tomorrow."], [2, "Day 2: 0 tickets closed. Strike 1.\nMistake: Wasted steps re-saving the same fix for ALD-104 without verifying or closing.\nLesson: Edit once, run reproduce to confirm, then close immediately. Avoid redundant tool calls.\nProcess: Verify fix with reproduce tool before closing. Do not repeat edits.\nGoal: Close ALD-104 first thing tomorrow, then ALD-112. Avoid second strike."], [3, "Day 3: 1 ticket closed (ALD-106 fixed). Target met.\nLesson: Alex's note held for tags (helper file), but emails.py appears direct.\nProcess: ALD-115 needs strip() in normalize_email. Fix identified.\nGoal: Close ALD-115 first thing tomorrow. Avoid second strike."]], "E05": [[1, "Closed ALD-118. Bug was in averages.py (helper), not scores.py as reproduce tool claimed. Alex's note (W-2) is correct; Sam's (W-1) is misleading.\nALD-119 pending: rota.py on_call week 1 returns 'Ben' instead of 'Ana'. Suspect off-by-one error (week 1 should map to index 0). Fix this first tomorrow to aim for the bonus.\nMet daily target (1/2)."], [2, "Day 2: Closed ALD-108. Bug was in byte_fmt.py (helper), not sizes.py as reproduce tool claimed. Alex's note (W-2) is reliable; Sam's (W-1) is not.\nALD-109 pending: words.py counts punctuation as words. Input 'Fix login - urgent !' returns 5 instead of 3. Fix splitting logic to ignore non-alphanumeric chars.\nMet daily target (1/2). Aim for bonus tomorrow by clearing ALD-109 first."], [3, "Day 3: Closed ALD-114. Bug was in day_diff.py (helper), not date_math.py as reproduce tool claimed. Alex's note (W-2) is correct; Sam's (W-1) is misleading.\nALD-120 closed as cannot_reproduce; growth.percent_change worked as expected.\nMet daily target (2/2). Bonus earned. No pending tickets for tomorrow. Start fresh on new assignments."]], "E06": [[1, "Closed ALD-107. Alex's wiki tip was right\u2014the bug was in the helper file (math_utils.py), not the file named by the reproduce tool. ALD-117 carries over; names.split_name seems to split on the first space instead of the last. Need to fix logic in names.py first thing. Met daily target (1/2)."], [2, "Day 2: Closed both tickets (ALD-123 cannot_reproduce, ALD-115 fixed). ALD-115 confirmed Alex's tip: the bug was in the helper (address_rules.py), not the file named by the reproduce tool (emails.py). Sam's shortcut doesn't hold up. Tomorrow: always check helper dependencies first before editing the named file."], [3, "Day 3: Closed both tickets (ALD-118 fixed, ALD-121 cannot_reproduce). Earned bonus. ALD-118 confirmed Alex's tip again\u2014the bug was in the helper (averages.py), not the file named by the reproduce tool (scores.py). Logic was dividing by len(values) instead of sum(weights). ALD-121 didn't reproduce when ran through the tool, so closed as cannot_reproduce per handbook. Sam's shortcut still unreliable. Tomorrow: always check helper dependencies first."]], "E07": [[1, "ALD-112 closed. Alex's helper-file tip worked well on csv_split.py.\nALD-102 pending: pages.py paginate() offset error.\nPage 1, size 2 returned [3, 4] vs expected [1, 2].\nLikely math error: page*size instead of (page-1)*size.\nPlan: Fix pages.py first thing tomorrow to secure bonus."], [2, "Day 2: Strike 1. 0 closes. ALD-104 edit failed.\nALD-104 pending: time_parse.py parse_duration() regex error.\nMinutes regex r\"(\\d)m\" captures single digit only. '1h30m' reads 0 mins.\nFix: change to r\"(\\d+)m\".\nALD-114: Not started.\nPlan: Apply ALD-104 fix first thing. Verify and close. Then start ALD-114."], [3, "Day 3: Bonus earned. 2 closes. ALD-101 fixed: text_rules.py split() vs split(\" \") removed stray dashes. ALD-122 closed cannot_reproduce: reproduce tool matched expected output. Strikes: 1. No pending tickets. Plan: Fresh start tomorrow. Maintain momentum."]], "E08": [[1, "Day 1 complete. Met target (1/2). ALD-108 fixed in byte_fmt.py (loop condition >= 1024). Alex's wiki note on helper files was spot on. ALD-124 didn't reproduce via tool, closed as cannot_reproduce. Reminder: always run reproduce tool before marking cannot_reproduce."], [2, "Day 2: Day 2 complete. Met target (1/2). ALD-104 fixed in time_parse.py (regex minutes \\d+). Alex's wiki note on helper files was spot on. ALD-115 pending: emails.py needs strip() for whitespace. Start there tomorrow."], [3, "Day 3 complete. Met target (1/2). ALD-102 fixed in slicing.py (page calc off-by-one, start index). Alex's wiki note on helper files was useful. ALD-119 pending: rota.py returns wrong person for week 1 (expected Ana, got Ben). Likely off-by-one index error. Start there tomorrow."]]}, "next_id": 9, "strikes": {"E04": 1, "E07": 1}, "bonuses": {"E01": 1, "E03": 1, "E04": 1, "E08": 1, "E06": 2, "E05": 1, "E07": 1}, "handover": {}, "yesterday": {"E01": {"done": 1, "strike": false, "bonus": false}, "E02": {"done": 1, "strike": false, "bonus": false}, "E03": {"done": 1, "strike": false, "bonus": false}, "E04": {"done": 1, "strike": false, "bonus": false}, "E05": {"done": 2, "strike": false, "bonus": true}, "E06": {"done": 2, "strike": false, "bonus": true}, "E07": {"done": 2, "strike": false, "bonus": true}, "E08": {"done": 1, "strike": false, "bonus": false}}, "moved_off": 0, "office": {"tickets": {"E01": {"ALD-118": {"id": "ALD-118", "status": "closed", "reproduced": true, "reproduced_first": true, "edited": true, "actions": 7, "day_assigned": 1, "tried_other_input": false, "helper_read_first": true, "entry_edited": false, "helper_edited": true, "own_input_after_edit": false}, "ALD-125": {"id": "ALD-125", "status": "closed", "reproduced": true, "reproduced_first": true, "edited": false, "actions": 3, "day_assigned": 1, "tried_other_input": false, "helper_read_first": false, "entry_edited": false, "helper_edited": false, "own_input_after_edit": false}, "ALD-105": {"id": "ALD-105", "status": "unfinished", "reproduced": true, "reproduced_first": true, "edited": false, "actions": 4, "day_assigned": 2, "tried_other_input": false, "helper_read_first": false, "entry_edited": false, "helper_edited": false, "own_input_after_edit": false}, "ALD-101": {"id": "ALD-101", "status": "closed", "reproduced": true, "reproduced_first": true, "edited": true, "actions": 6, "day_assign